<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.KOREA'S DACOM H1 NET FALLS SHARPLY.</title>
<headline>S.KOREA'S DACOM H1 NET FALLS SHARPLY.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net				  5.2  vs   10.8</p>
<p>    Turnover			 319.0  vs  310.4</p>
<p>    Profit before tax		6.4  vs   13.0</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	1.5 (profit) vs 0.1 (loss)</p>
<p>NOTE - Dacom Corp, South Korea's one of two international and long distance call operators, attributed the drop in net profit to its rate cuts in December to win more subscribers.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
